{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_137","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A12 -B2 '1351|protected Windows cache|late hard|INHERIT_ONLY' LOGBOOK.md\"","aggregated_output":"6-## 2026-07-30\n7-\n8:### 1351 — A protected Windows cache must set the manager owner explicitly and pin identities across every seal transition\n9-\n10-- IMPLEMENTATION: `TASK-260720-8nxlgx` adds the Windows backend for the immutable `go-v1` build cache. Manager, SYSTEM and Builtin Administrators receive exact protected DACL profiles; lookup opens reparse points themselves, proves direct-child containment and stable file IDs, rejects alternate streams and link counts other than one, revalidates receipt/artifact hashes and sizes, and publishes a fully sealed same-volume staging tree with a non-replacing `MoveFileExW`.\n11-- PLATFORM FINDING: an elevated Windows token can create new objects owned by Builtin Administrators rather than the current manager SID. Creation and sealing therefore set the current SID as owner explicitly. Later cleanup must be DACL-only: a sealed manager ACE retains implicit `WRITE_DAC`, but deliberately lacks `WRITE_OWNER`.\n12-- RACE FINDING: Windows keeps an entry directory non-renamable while descendant handles are pinned even with delete sharing. The live containment negative case therefore replaces the artifact at its path while the lookup holds the original handle; the file-ID/path re-open mismatch forces an untrusted miss and exposes no candidate path or bytes.\n13-- EVIDENCE: native Windows backend suite 16/16 and full suite 783 passed / 144 skipped with a process-only PowerShell policy bypass; local cache contract 42 passed / 16 skipped, full suite 853 passed / 74 skipped, strict mypy 65 files, Ruff, build, Twine, compile and diff gates all exit 0.\n14-- ANOMALY: native full-repository mypy exits 1 on 51 pre-existing Windows platform-stub errors outside this backend. The task module itself passes `mypy --platform win32 --follow-im